    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 66 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag that returns `true` when an owner's city already holds between 40 and 49 owners (inclusive) \u2014 approaching the hard limit of 50, which remains unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean field to the `OwnerDto` schema (next to the existing `bulkSignupWarning`), which generates the `setCapacityWarning` setter on the DTO.\n\n2. **`CapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 a helper mirroring `BulkSignupWarning`. It counts owners in the owner's city (case-insensitively, matching `EnsureCityCapacity`'s grouping) and returns `true` when the count is in `[40, 49]`.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithExistingOwner`** \u2014 each now sets `capacityWarning` on the response DTO, so the flag is computed consistently across the GET, create (201), and idempotent-replay (200) paths.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 in `EnsureCityCapacity` was left untouched. The new `Cp54Tests` (warning at 40\u201349), the existing `Cp18Tests` (409 rejection at 50), and the full suite (66 tests) all pass.",
